{"version": 2, "width": 120, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1791381260, "idle_time_limit": 1.5, "title": "A report every Monday, with no scheduler (recorded from a real run; waits longer than 1.5 s are shortened to 1.5 s)", "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "dumb"}}
[0.072, "o", "# hooks.conf: admin-token = <secret>, allow-private-hosts = 1 (the receivers are on this machine), pg-* = a PostgreSQL\r\n"]
[0.072, "o", "$ hooks --config hooks.conf --port $PORT --dir $DATA &\r\n"]
[0.14, "o", "# the endpoint that wants the report\r\n$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X POST $URL/endpoints -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\" -d '{\"host\":\"127.0.0.1\",\"port\":'$REPORTS_PORT',\"types\":[\"report.due\"]}'\r\n"]
[0.145, "o", "{\"id\":0,\"host\":\"127.0.0.1\",\"scheme\":\"http\",\"port\":51471,\"secret\":\"whsec_…\",\"from\":\"now\",\"cursor\":0} [201]\r\n"]
[0.155, "o", "# part one: the real schedule, every Monday at 06:00 UTC\r\n"]
[0.155, "o", "$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X POST $URL/schedules -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\" -d '{\"expr\":\"0 6 * * 1\",\"type\":\"report.due\",\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"}}'\r\n"]
[0.159, "o", "{\"id\":1,\"expr\":\"0 6 * * 1\",\"type\":\"report.due\",\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"},\"enabled\":true,\"created_at\":1791381255,\"last_fired\":null,\"next_fire\":1791784800,\"next_fire_at\":\"2026-10-12T06:00:00Z\"} [201]\r\n"]
[0.178, "o", "ok: the next fire is a Monday, 06:00:00 UTC\r\n$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X DELETE $URL/schedules/$SCHEDULE -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\"\r\n"]
[0.183, "o", "{\"id\":1,\"deleted\":true} [200]\r\n"]
[0.184, "o", "# part two: the same, with seconds, so that it can be watched (a fire every 2 seconds)\r\n"]
[0.184, "o", "$ hooks --config hooks.conf --port $PORT --dir $DATA --cron-seconds 1 &\r\n"]
[0.253, "o", "$ python3 examples/receiver.py --name reports --port $REPORTS_PORT --secret-file reports.secret &\r\n"]
[0.317, "o", "$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X POST $URL/schedules -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\" -d '{\"expr\":\"*/2 * * * * *\",\"type\":\"report.due\",\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"}}'\r\n"]
[0.322, "o", "{\"id\":2,\"expr\":\"*/2 * * * * *\",\"type\":\"report.due\",\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"},\"enabled\":true,\"created_at\":1791381255,\"last_fired\":null,\"next_fire\":1791381256,\"next_fire_at\":\"2026-10-07T13:54:16Z\"} [201]\r\n"]
[0.331, "o", "# nothing else sends events: these are the fires\r\n"]
[1.831, "o", "  reports evt_1 signature ok (1 signature) {\"type\":\"report.due\",\"schedule\":2,\"scheduled_at\":1791381256,\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"}}\r\n  reports evt_2 signature ok (1 signature) {\"type\":\"report.due\",\"schedule\":2,\"scheduled_at\":1791381258,\"body\":{\"report\":\"weekly\"}}\r\n"]
[1.832, "o", "$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X DELETE $URL/schedules/$SCHEDULE -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\"\r\n"]
[1.836, "o", "{\"id\":2,\"deleted\":true} [200]\r\n"]
[1.837, "o", "ok: each fire carries the schedule's id, the second it was due and its body\r\n"]
[3.337, "o", "$ curl -s $URL/stats | grep -o '\"cron_fired\":[0-9]*'\r\n"]
[3.344, "o", "\"cron_fired\":2\r\n"]
[3.356, "o", "ok: the fires the service counted are the verified deliveries the receiver has: none lost, none doubled\r\n# a fire is an event like any other: it can be sent again, with the same webhook-id\r\n$ curl -s -w ' [%{http_code}]\\n' -X POST $URL/events/1/replay -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN\"\r\n"]
[3.362, "o", "{\"event\":1,\"endpoints\":[0]} [202]\r\n"]
[3.372, "o", "  reports evt_1 signature ok (1 signature) duplicate\r\n"]
[3.373, "o", "ok: the replay of the first fire was recognised as a repeat\r\n"]
